"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#check-the-publication","content":"Check the publication"},"739":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-23","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","content":"A certification authority (CA) binds identities to public keys through signed certificates. In Lamassu you can create a new hierarchy, use a key already in the KMS or incorporate an external CA."},"740":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-24","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","content":"To design a full chain or replace an authority in production, see CA hierarchy and rotation. If you need to standardize what each authority can sign, use Certificate profiles."},"741":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-25","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#choose-a-flow","content":"**New CA with a new key:** create a root of trust from scratch. Lamassu generates and keeps the key pair."},"742":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-26","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#choose-a-flow","content":"**New CA from the KMS:** reuse a key already registered in the platform."},"743":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-27","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#choose-a-flow","content":"**Import a CA with its private key:** incorporate an external authority that Lamassu can issue with."},"744":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-28","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#choose-a-flow","content":"**Import only the certificate:** add an authority for building chains and validating, but not for issuing."},"745":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-29","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#choose-a-flow","content":"First time here? Follow Create your first CA to complete the minimal journey."},"746":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-30","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#before-you-begin","content":"Decide whether the CA will be a root or an intermediate."},"747":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-31","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#before-you-begin","content":"Choose the engine that will keep the key."},"748":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-32","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#before-you-begin","content":"Define a validity longer than that of the certificates it will issue."},"749":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-33","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#before-you-begin","content":"For an intermediate CA, make sure the parent CA is active."},"750":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-34","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#open-the-wizard","content":"In **Certification Authorities**, select **Create New CA** and choose to generate a new key pair."},"751":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-35","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#configure-the-key","content":"Select the cryptographic engine, the algorithm and the size or curve. Lamassu supports RSA and EC keys according to the engine's capabilities."},"752":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-36","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#configure-the-key","content":"For RSA you can choose 1024, 2048, 3072 or 4096 bits. For EC, the P-256, P-384 and P-521 curves are available."},"753":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-37","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#choose-the-ca-type","content":"Select **Root CA** for a self-signed authority or **Intermediate CA** for an authority signed by another CA. In the latter case, choose the issuing CA."},"754":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-38","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#define-the-identity","content":"Enter a unique **CA Name**. This name becomes the certificate's `Common Name`. Complete the Distinguished Name fields your policy requires:"},"755":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-39","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#define-the-identity","content":"`C`: two-letter ISO 3166-1 country code."},"756":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-40","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#define-the-identity","content":"`ST`: state or province."},"757":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-41","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#define-the-identity","content":"`L`: locality."},"758":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-42","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#define-the-identity","content":"`O`: organization."},"759":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-43","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#define-the-identity","content":"`OU`: organizational unit."},"760":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-44","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#define-the-identity","content":"The CA's internal identifier is generated automatically and cannot be changed."},"761":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-45","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#configure-validity-and-uses","content":"Define **CA Certificate Expiration** and **Default End-Entity Certificate Issuance Expiration**. You can express a duration (`5y 8w 4d`), pick a date or use the maximum allowed date."},"762":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-46","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#configure-validity-and-uses","content":"Select an existing issuance profile or configure the `Key Usage` and `Extended Key Usage` in the form. If you don't choose a profile, Lamassu applies the default basic usages."},"763":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-47","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#create-and-verify","content":"Confirm the form. The CA should appear in the inventory with its PEM certificate, status, expiration date and list of issued certificates."},"764":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-48","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#create-and-verify","content":"A CA cannot issue certificates that outlive its own expiration date. Leave enough margin to renew or replace the authority without interrupting consumers."},"765":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-49","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#use-a-key-from-the-kms","content":"Select &#x2A;*Create New CA (Existing Key)** when the key is already registered in Lamassu. The wizard first asks for the backing key and then shows the same configuration of type, identity, validity and profile."},"766":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-50","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#use-a-key-from-the-kms","content":"This flow is useful when the key was previously created in an HSM, imported through BYOK or must be reused under a specific custody policy."},"767":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-51","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#import-an-external-ca","content":"Importing preserves an authority created outside Lamassu."},"768":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-52","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#select-the-engine","content":"Choose the engine that will keep the imported key."},"769":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-53","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#load-the-material","content":"Provide the CA certificate and the private key in PEM format. For a subordinate CA, optionally add the validation chain."},"770":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-54","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#define-the-default-issuance","content":"Configure the validity that end-entity certificates will receive when a request does not specify another duration."},"771":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-55","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#verify-the-import","content":"Lamassu checks that the certificate belongs to a CA and that the material is coherent before registering it."},"772":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-56","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#verify-the-import","content":"If you don't have the private key, import only the certificate. The authority can take part in chains of trust and validation processes, but it cannot issue certificates from Lamassu."},"773":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-57","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#inspect-an-authority","content":"Open a CA from the inventory to review:"},"774":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-58","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#inspect-an-authority","content":"Status and validity period."},"775":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-59","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#inspect-an-authority","content":"Certificate and chain in PEM format."},"776":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-60","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#inspect-an-authority","content":"Number of active, expired and revoked certificates."},"777":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-61","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#inspect-an-authority","content":"Certificates issued in **Issued Certificates**."},"778":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-62","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#inspect-an-authority","content":"The CRL linked to the authority."},"779":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-63","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#inspect-an-authority","content":"Metadata and the associated cryptographic engine."},"780":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-64","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#inspect-an-authority","content":"You can filter the inventory by name, status and CA type."},"781":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-65","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#issue-certificates","content":"You can start an issuance from **Issued Certificates**, from a CA's action menu or from the global certificate inventory."},"782":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-66","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#issue-certificates","content":"**Generate Key & CSR in Browser** is useful for a manual operation or a quick test. The browser generates the key and you must download it at the end."},"783":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-67","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#issue-certificates","content":"**Upload Existing CSR** is the right option when the key must remain on the target system. Lamassu receives the request but never the private key."},"784":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-68","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#issue-certificates","content":"Follow Issue your first certificate for the guided flow. Certificate management explains the inventory, inspection and revocation."},"785":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-69","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#revoke-a-ca","content":"Revoking a CA invalidates trust in the certificates it issued and can interrupt devices and services. The action is irreversible."},"786":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-70","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#assess-the-impact","content":"Identify the certificates, devices and consumers that depend on the CA. Prepare a replacement authority and chain when necessary."},"787":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-71","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#start-the-revocation","content":"Open the authority and select **Revoke CA**. Choose the reason that describes the incident, for example `KeyCompromise`, `CACompromise`, `Superseded` or `CessationOfOperation`."},"788":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-72","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#confirm-the-identity","content":"Type the CA's name exactly to enable **Confirm Revocation**."},"789":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-73","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#check-the-publication","content":"The status should change to **REVOKED** and the CRL should reflect the new information. The CA can no longer issue certificates."},"790":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-74","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#check-the-publication","content":"Permanent deletion is only available after revoking. Delete the record only when your retention and audit policy allows it."},"791":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","type":"page","content":"Certificate profiles","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Platform","Operate Lamassu"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles"},"792":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","content":"Define reusable policies to issue consistent certificates and constrain accepted keys."},"793":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#what-a-profile-controls","content":"What a profile controls"},"794":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#validity","content":"Validity"},"795":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-3","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#ca-certificate-or-end-entity-certificate","content":"CA certificate or end-entity certificate"},"796":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-4","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#key-usage-and-extended-key-usage","content":"Key Usage and Extended Key Usage"},"797":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-5","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#subject","content":"Subject"},"798":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-6","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#csr-extensions","content":"CSR extensions"},"799":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-7","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#cryptographic-constraints","content":"Cryptographic constraints"},"800":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-8","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#profile-precedence","content":"Profile precedence"},"801":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-9","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#create-a-profile","content":"Create a profile"},"802":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-10","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#define-a-single-purpose","content":"Define a single purpose"},"803":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-11","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#choose-the-validity","content":"Choose the validity"},"804":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-12","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#fix-usages-and-subject","content":"Fix usages and subject"},"805":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-13","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#constrain-the-keys","content":"Constrain the keys"},"806":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-14","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#attach-it-and-test","content":"Attach it and test"},"807":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-15","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#design-examples","content":"Design examples"},"808":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-16","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#changes-and-deletion","content":"Changes and deletion"},"809":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-17","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","content":"An issuance profile turns a certificate policy into reusable configuration. Instead of deciding validity, subject, extensions and algorithms on every request, you define once what is allowed and attach the profile to a CA, a DMS or a specific issuance."},"810":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-18","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#validity","content":"You can express the lifetime as a duration from the moment of issuance or as a fixed end date. A duration works well for recurring identities; a common date is useful to make a whole batch end before a migration or retirement."},"811":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-19","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#validity","content":"The end date must never outlive the issuing CA."},"812":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-20","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#ca-certificate-or-end-entity-certificate","content":"`Sign as CA` sets `IsCA` and the basic constraints needed for an authority. Enable it only in profiles intended to create or reissue subordinate CAs."},"813":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-21","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#key-usage-and-extended-key-usage","content":"The profile can enforce usages such as `DigitalSignature`, `KeyEncipherment`, `CertSign`, `CRLSign`, `ClientAuth`, `ServerAuth` or `OCSPSigning`."},"814":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-22","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#key-usage-and-extended-key-usage","content":"If you enable **Honor Key Usage** or **Honor Extended Key Usages**, Lamassu keeps the values requested by the CSR. If you disable them, it replaces them with the ones defined in the profile."},"815":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-23","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#key-usage-and-extended-key-usage","content":"Do not enable the `Honor…` options for untrusted requests unless another component validates those fields. Otherwise, the requester may choose broader capabilities than intended."},"816":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-24","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#subject","content":"With **Honor Subject**, the certificate keeps the subject of the CSR. Without that option, Lamassu applies the profile's `CN`, `O`, `OU`, `C`, `ST` and `L`. If the profile does not define a `Common Name`, the requested CN is kept."},"817":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-25","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#csr-extensions","content":"With **Honor Extensions**, Lamassu filters the additional requested extensions and keeps only SAN. Without that option, it discards the CSR's additional extensions."},"818":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-26","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#csr-extensions","content":"This behavior allows accepting DNS, IP, email or URI as alternative identities without accepting arbitrary extensions."},"819":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-27","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#cryptographic-constraints","content":"The cryptographic enforcement can:"},"820":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-28","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#cryptographic-constraints","content":"allow or block RSA keys;"},"821":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-29","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#cryptographic-constraints","content":"limit the supported RSA sizes;"},"822":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-30","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#cryptographic-constraints","content":"allow or block ECDSA keys;"},"823":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-31","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#cryptographic-constraints","content":"limit the supported ECDSA sizes or curves."},"824":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-32","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#cryptographic-constraints","content":"When it is enabled, Lamassu checks the public key before creating a CA or signing a CSR. A key whose type or size is not listed in the profile is rejected."},"825":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-33","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#profile-precedence","content":"In operations that accept multiple sources, Lamassu resolves the profile in this order:"},"826":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-34","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#profile-precedence","content":"The profile sent within the operation."},"827":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-35","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#profile-precedence","content":"The profile identifier sent in the operation."},"828":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-36","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#profile-precedence","content":"The default profile associated with the CA."},"829":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-37","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#profile-precedence","content":"A DMS can also reference its own issuance profile. This way, several fleets can use the same CA with different policies."},"830":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-38","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#define-a-single-purpose","content":"Separate, for example, mTLS devices, servers and intermediate CAs. A small, specific profile is easier to review than one that allows every use."},"831":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-39","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#choose-the-validity","content":"Align the duration with the fleet's real renewal capacity. Leave margin against the CA's expiration."},"832":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-40","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#fix-usages-and-subject","content":"For a device that authenticates as a client, the usual starting point is `DigitalSignature` and `ClientAuth`. Add `ServerAuth` or `KeyEncipherment` only if the protocol needs it."},"833":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-41","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#constrain-the-keys","content":"Enable cryptographic enforcement and list only algorithms and sizes compatible with your policy and your devices."},"834":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-42","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#attach-it-and-test","content":"Attach the profile to a CA or DMS. Issue a test certificate and check subject, SAN, KU, EKU, basic constraints and dates with an independent X.509 tool."},"835":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-43","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#design-examples","content":"**mTLS device**\\\nEnd-entity certificate, short validity, `DigitalSignature`, `ClientAuth`, subject controlled by the DMS and SAN allowed when it identifies the device."},"836":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-44","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#design-examples","content":"**TLS server**\\\nEnd-entity certificate, `DigitalSignature`, `ServerAuth` and mandatory SAN with the names clients will use."},"837":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-45","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#design-examples","content":"**Intermediate CA**\\\n`Sign as CA`, `CertSign` and `CRLSign`, validity longer than its end-entity certificates and stricter cryptographic constraints."},"838":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-46","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#design-examples","content":"These are starting patterns, not a universal policy. Always verify the requirements of the protocol, the consumer and the applicable regulatory framework."},"839":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-47","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#changes-and-deletion","content":"Updating a profile affects future issuances; it does not modify already-signed certificates. Test changes before applying them to a CA in production and keep the operational justification."},"840":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles-48","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-profiles#changes-and-deletion","content":"Before deleting a profile, check that no CA or DMS depends on it. If you want to replace it, create the new version, update the references and perform a test issuance before retiring the old one."},"841":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-validation","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-validation","type":"page","content":"Certificate validation","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Platform","Operate Lamassu"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-validation"},"842":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-validation-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-validation","content":"Publish the status of identities through OCSP and CRL."},"843":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-validation-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-validation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-validation#choose-a-mechanism","content":"Choose a mechanism"},"844":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-validation-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-validation","content":"Issuance proves who signed a certificate; validation tells you whether it should still be accepted. Lamassu publishes status through two complementary mechanisms."},"845":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-validation-3","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-validation#choose-a-mechanism","content":"Use **OCSP** when the consumer is online and needs to check the latest status of a specific certificate."},"846":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-validation-4","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-validation#choose-a-mechanism","content":"Use a **CRL** when validation must happen locally, offline or over a high volume of certificates. The consumer periodically downloads a signed list and keeps it until the next update."},"847":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-validation-5","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-validation#choose-a-mechanism","content":"Many environments use both: OCSP as the primary check and a CRL as the local or fallback mechanism."},"848":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-validation-6","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-validation#choose-a-mechanism","content":"<Card title=\"Online validation with OCSP\" description=\"Query Good, Revoked and Unknown statuses in real time.\" href=\"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp\" />"},"849":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-validation-7","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificate-validation#choose-a-mechanism","content":"<Card title=\"Revocation lists\" description=\"Generate, publish and distribute CRLs per authority.\" href=\"/docs/platform/pki/crl\" />"},"850":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates","type":"page","content":"Certificates","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Platform","Operate Lamassu"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates"},"851":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates","content":"Inspect, download and revoke the certificates issued by Lamassu."},"852":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates#find-a-certificate","content":"Find a certificate"},"853":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates#download-the-certificate","content":"Download the certificate"},"854":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates-3","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates#revoke-a-certificate","content":"Revoke a certificate"},"855":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates-4","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates#open-the-action","content":"Open the action"},"856":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates-5","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates#choose-a-reason","content":"Choose a reason"},"857":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates-6","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates#confirm-and-verify","content":"Confirm and verify"},"858":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates-7","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates#continue","content":"Continue"},"859":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates-8","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates","content":"The certificate inventory offers a global view of the identities issued by all authorities. You can also open **Issued Certificates** inside a CA to limit the view to that issuer."},"860":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates-9","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates#find-a-certificate","content":"Open **Certificates** and filter by:"},"861":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates-10","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates#find-a-certificate","content":"Subject's `Common Name`."},"862":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates-11","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates#find-a-certificate","content":"Serial number."},"863":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates-12","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates#find-a-certificate","content":"Status."},"864":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates-13","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates#find-a-certificate","content":"Issuing authority."},"865":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates-14","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates#find-a-certificate","content":"Use **Quick Inspect** for a quick check or **View Details** to see the subject, SANs, usages, chain, validity period and full metadata."},"866":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates-15","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates#download-the-certificate","content":"The download action delivers the certificate in PEM format. If the certificate was issued from an external CSR, the private key stays on the system that generated that CSR. If it was generated in the browser, the key was only available when the issuance finished."},"867":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates-16","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates#revoke-a-certificate","content":"Revoke an identity when the key has been compromised, the subject is no longer authorized or the certificate must stop being accepted before it expires."},"868":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates-17","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates#open-the-action","content":"In the inventory or detail view, select **Revoke Certificate**."},"869":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates-18","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates#choose-a-reason","content":"Select the reason that represents the incident. This information is published in OCSP and in the CRL."},"870":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates-19","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates#confirm-and-verify","content":"Confirm the operation and check that the status is **Revoked**. If the CA regenerates the CRL upon revocation, also verify that a new version exists."},"871":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates-20","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates#confirm-and-verify","content":"A revocation with the reason `CertificateHold` can be reactivated. All other reasons produce a final revocation."},"872":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates-21","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates#continue","content":"<Card title=\"Validate with OCSP\" description=\"Query the status of a certificate in real time.\" href=\"/docs/platform/pki/ocsp\" />"},"873":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates-22","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/certificates#continue","content":"<Card title=\"Distribute a CRL\" description=\"Publish the status for offline validation.\" href=\"/docs/platform/pki/crl\" />"},"874":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/architecture","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/architecture","type":"page","content":"Platform architecture","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Platform","Concepts"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/architecture"},"875":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/architecture-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/architecture","content":"Lamassu components and how control, keys, issuance and devices relate."},"876":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/architecture-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/architecture#control-plane","content":"Control plane"},"877":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/architecture-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/architecture#key-custody-and-cryptographic-operations","content":"Key custody and cryptographic operations"},"878":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/architecture-3","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/architecture#issuance-and-enrollment","content":"Issuance and enrollment"},"879":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/architecture-4","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/architecture#status-and-validation","content":"Status and validation"},"880":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/architecture-5","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/architecture#platform-dependencies","content":"Platform dependencies"},"881":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/architecture-6","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/architecture","content":"Lamassu deploys as a set of independent services. This separation keeps every component from needing direct access to private keys and lets each capability scale according to load."},"882":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/architecture-7","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/architecture","content":"Switch to the low level to see the internals of the Lamassu platform box (CA, KMS, DMS, Device Manager, VA, Alerts, AWS IoT connector, Job Manager and the console/API), and to medium to see it as a single platform alongside its external dependencies."},"883":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/architecture-8","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/architecture#control-plane","content":"The console and the APIs manage authorities, certificates, DMSs, devices, alerts and configuration. Domain events allow connectors and automations to react to changes without continuously polling the platform."},"884":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/architecture-9","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/architecture#key-custody-and-cryptographic-operations","content":"The KMS offers a common interface over software engines, PKCS#11 and cloud providers. The selected engine keeps the key or delegates the cryptographic operation without the other services knowing its implementation."},"885":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/architecture-10","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/architecture#issuance-and-enrollment","content":"The CA service issues certificates and maintains the relationship with its authority. The DMS applies the enrollment rules and exposes the EST flows so a device can request or renew an identity."},"886":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/architecture-11","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/architecture#status-and-validation","content":"Device Manager keeps the operational view of the device and its history. The Validation Authority publishes OCSP and CRLs so other systems can decide whether to trust a presented certificate."},"887":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/architecture-12","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/architecture#platform-dependencies","content":"In a self-managed deployment, Lamassu uses PostgreSQL for persistence, RabbitMQ for messaging and an OIDC provider for authentication. See the deployment architecture for how the services are published on Kubernetes."},"888":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","type":"page","content":"Certificate lifecycle","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Platform","Concepts"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle"},"889":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","content":"Issuance, use, renewal, revocation and retirement of certificates in Lamassu."},"890":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#the-full-journey","content":"The full journey"},"891":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#request","content":"Request"},"892":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-3","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#issuance","content":"Issuance"},"893":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-4","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#use-and-monitoring","content":"Use and monitoring"},"894":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-5","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#renewal-or-re-enrollment","content":"Renewal or re-enrollment"},"895":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-6","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#revocation-or-retirement","content":"Revocation or retirement"},"896":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-7","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#certificate-states","content":"Certificate states"},"897":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-8","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#renewal-and-revocation-are-not-equivalent","content":"Renewal and revocation are not equivalent"},"898":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-9","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#effect-of-revoking-a-ca","content":"Effect of revoking a CA"},"899":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-10","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#what-you-should-watch","content":"What you should watch"},"900":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-11","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","content":"Issuing a certificate is only the beginning. During its useful life you must check its validity, renew it before it expires and retire it when it stops being trustworthy. Lamassu keeps the certificate, its issuing CA, its status and, when it belongs to a device, the identity it is linked to."},"901":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-12","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#request","content":"The requester generates a key and a CSR. In the recommended flows, the private key stays in the device, browser or cryptographic engine that created it."},"902":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-13","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#issuance","content":"The CA signs the CSR. The issuance profile determines the validity, uses, subject, allowed extensions and cryptographic constraints."},"903":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-14","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#use-and-monitoring","content":"The certificate enters the `ACTIVE` state. Lamassu monitors its `Not After` date; the cryptographic monitoring job marks certificates that have expired as `EXPIRED`."},"904":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-15","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#renewal-or-re-enrollment","content":"A new certificate is issued before the previous one expires. In a DMS you can open preventive and critical windows so the device re-enrolls through EST."},"905":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-16","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#revocation-or-retirement","content":"If the identity stops being trustworthy, Lamassu records the reason and time of revocation. OCSP and CRLs let consumers learn that status."},"906":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-17","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#certificate-states","content":"Lamassu persists four X.509 states:"},"907":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-18","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#certificate-states","content":"**`ACTIVE`**: the certificate is enabled and within its validity period."},"908":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-19","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#certificate-states","content":"**`EXPIRED`**: it has passed its expiration date. The monitor detects this periodically; it is not a state that should be assigned manually."},"909":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-20","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#certificate-states","content":"**`REVOKED`**: it was invalidated before expiring, with a reason and a timestamp."},"910":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-21","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#certificate-states","content":"**`INACTIVE`**: it is disabled without representing a definitive revocation."},"911":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-22","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#certificate-states","content":"The device view may add operational states such as missing identity, pending renewal, expiring soon or decommissioned. These are an interpretation of the device's status and its certificates, not new X.509 states."},"912":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-23","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#renewal-and-revocation-are-not-equivalent","content":"**Renewal** creates a successor certificate for an identity that remains valid. **Revocation** communicates that the current certificate must no longer be accepted. Renew to maintain continuity; revoke in response to compromise, retirement or a change that invalidates the identity."},"913":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-24","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#renewal-and-revocation-are-not-equivalent","content":"Only a revocation with the reason `CertificateHold` can be undone. A revocation with any other reason is final in Lamassu."},"914":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-25","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#renewal-and-revocation-are-not-equivalent","content":"The **Reissue CA** operation generates another certificate for the same key and links both serial numbers through metadata. It is not a key rotation. To change the key, create a successor CA and perform a migration with an overlapping period."},"915":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-26","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#effect-of-revoking-a-ca","content":"Revoking a CA is a cascading operation. Lamassu revokes its child CAs and the certificates it issued, with the reason `CessationOfOperation`. The propagation continues down the hierarchy."},"916":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-27","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#effect-of-revoking-a-ca","content":"Before confirming:"},"917":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-28","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#effect-of-revoking-a-ca","content":"Identify DMSs, devices and services that trust that chain."},"918":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-29","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#effect-of-revoking-a-ca","content":"Distribute the new chain of trust."},"919":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-30","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#effect-of-revoking-a-ca","content":"Reissue the necessary identities."},"920":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-31","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#effect-of-revoking-a-ca","content":"Check OCSP and CRL from a real consumer."},"921":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-32","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#effect-of-revoking-a-ca","content":"Revoke the old CA once no legitimate traffic remains."},"922":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-33","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#effect-of-revoking-a-ca","content":"Decommissioning a device revokes its certificates and prevents it from obtaining new identities. Use this action only when the device is being retired permanently."},"923":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-34","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#what-you-should-watch","content":"Certificates entering the preventive or critical renewal window."},"924":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-35","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#what-you-should-watch","content":"Repeated enrollment or re-enrollment failures."},"925":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-36","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#what-you-should-watch","content":"Status changes and revocation reasons."},"926":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-37","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#what-you-should-watch","content":"OCSP and CRL publication and validity."},"927":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-38","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#what-you-should-watch","content":"Dependencies still presenting a replaced certificate."},"928":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle-39","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle#what-you-should-watch","content":"The device history relates its previous and current identities. For administrative changes and mutation errors, see Audit logs."},"929":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary","type":"page","content":"Glossary","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Platform","Concepts"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary"},"930":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary","content":"PKI, certificate and identity management terms used in Lamassu."},"931":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary#ac","content":"A–C"},"932":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary#dk","content":"D–K"},"933":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary-3","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary#mr","content":"M–R"},"934":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary-4","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary#sz","content":"S–Z"},"935":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary-5","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary#ac","content":"**AKI (Authority Key Identifier)**\\\nIdentifier of the public key of the authority that signed a certificate. It helps build the chain toward the correct issuer."},"936":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary-6","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary#ac","content":"**Anchor of trust**\\\nA certificate, usually from a root CA, that a consumer explicitly accepts as the endpoint of a chain."},"937":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary-7","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary#ac","content":"**CA (Certification Authority)**\\\nAuthority that signs certificates and binds an identity to a public key."},"938":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary-8","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary#ac","content":"**Intermediate CA**\\\nA CA signed by another authority. Used to issue without exposing the root to daily operation."},"939":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary-9","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary#ac","content":"**Root CA**\\\nA self-signed CA that starts a hierarchy of trust."},"940":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary-10","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary#ac","content":"**X.509 certificate**\\\nA signed document containing a public key, a subject, an issuer, a validity period and extensions that constrain its use."},"941":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary-11","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary#ac","content":"**CRL (Certificate Revocation List)**\\\nSigned list of revoked certificates published by a CA."},"942":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary-12","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary#ac","content":"**CSR (Certificate Signing Request)**\\\nPKCS#10 request containing a public key and requested attributes. Signing the CSR proves possession of the corresponding private key."},"943":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary-13","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary#dk","content":"**DMS (Device Management Service)**\\\nConfiguration that groups registration, enrollment, re-enrollment, issuance and CA distribution rules for a fleet."},"944":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary-14","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary#dk","content":"**Distinguished Name (DN)**\\\nSet of subject or issuer attributes, such as `CN`, `O`, `OU`, `C`, `ST` and `L`."},"945":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary-15","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary#dk","content":"**EST (Enrollment over Secure Transport)**\\\nProtocol defined in RFC 7030 to obtain CAs, enroll and re-enroll certificates over HTTPS."},"946":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary-16","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary#dk","content":"**Extended Key Usage (EKU)**\\\nExtension that constrains purposes such as client authentication, server authentication, code signing or OCSP."},"947":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary-17","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary#dk","content":"**Device identity**\\\nRelationship between a device and one of its certificates. A device can keep a history of identities."},"948":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary-18","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary#dk","content":"**Identity slot**\\\nLogical position on a device where Lamassu binds an active or historical identity."},"949":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary-19","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary#dk","content":"**JITP (Just-in-Time Provisioning)**\\\nAutomatic registration of a device when it successfully completes its first enrollment."},"950":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary-20","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary#dk","content":"**KMS (Key Management Service)**\\\nLamassu service that normalizes key generation, import and use across different cryptographic engines."},"951":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary-21","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary#dk","content":"**Key Usage**\\\nX.509 extension that allows basic operations such as digital signature, key encryption or certificate signing."},"952":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary-22","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary#mr","content":"**mTLS (Mutual TLS)**\\\nTLS where both client and server present certificates. A DMS can use the client certificate as an authentication method."},"953":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary-23","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary#mr","content":"**OCSP (Online Certificate Status Protocol)**\\\nProtocol for querying online whether a certificate is valid, revoked or unknown."},"954":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary-24","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary#mr","content":"**Issuance profile**\\\nReusable policy that defines how Lamassu builds a certificate and which keys it accepts."},"955":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary-25","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary#mr","content":"**Principal**\\\nOperator or API client identity recognized by the authorization service. Lamassu supports OIDC and X.509 principals."},"956":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary-26","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary#mr","content":"**Policy**\\\nSet of permissions assignable to one or more principals."},"957":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary-27","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary#mr","content":"**RA (Registration Authority)**\\\nComponent that verifies the requester before asking a CA to issue. The DMS plays this role in device enrollment flows."},"958":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary-28","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary#mr","content":"**Relying party**\\\nConsuming system that decides whether to accept a presented certificate."},"959":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary-29","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary#mr","content":"**Revocation**\\\nInvalidation of a certificate before its expiration date."},"960":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary-30","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary#sz","content":"**SAN (Subject Alternative Name)**\\\nExtension that adds identities such as DNS names, IP addresses, emails or URIs."},"961":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary-31","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary#sz","content":"**SKI (Subject Key Identifier)**\\\nIdentifier derived from the public key of the certificate itself."},"962":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary-32","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary#sz","content":"**VA (Validation Authority)**\\\nLamassu service responsible for OCSP responses and the generation or publication of CRLs."},"963":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary-33","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary#sz","content":"**Renewal window**\\\nPeriod before expiration during which a device may or must request another identity."},"964":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary-34","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/glossary#sz","content":"Missing an operational term? Check How Lamassu works and the Trust model first, where these concepts appear connected."},"965":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/overview","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/overview","type":"page","content":"How Lamassu works","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Platform","Concepts"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/overview"},"966":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/overview-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/overview","content":"The mental model of trust, keys, certificates and devices."},"967":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/overview-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/overview#the-model-in-five-pieces","content":"The model in five pieces"},"968":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/overview-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/overview#from-onboarding-to-operation","content":"From onboarding to operation"},"969":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/overview-3","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/overview","content":"Lamassu connects three elements: a **root of trust**, an **issuance policy** and an **entity that needs to prove its identity**. The platform coordinates these elements throughout the certificate lifecycle."},"970":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/overview-4","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/overview#the-model-in-five-pieces","content":"**Cryptographic engine.** Generates or safeguards keys and executes private-key operations without exposing key material to the rest of the services."},"971":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/overview-5","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/overview#the-model-in-five-pieces","content":"**Certification Authority (CA).** Signs certificates and establishes the chain of trust."},"972":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/overview-6","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/overview#the-model-in-five-pieces","content":"**Device Management Service (DMS).** Defines how the devices of a fleet are registered, authenticated and renewed."},"973":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/overview-7","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/overview#the-model-in-five-pieces","content":"**Device.** Keeps its private key and presents the certificate to prove its identity."},"974":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/overview-8","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/overview#the-model-in-five-pieces","content":"**Validation Authority (VA).** Publishes the status of certificates through OCSP and CRL."},"975":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/overview-9","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/overview#from-onboarding-to-operation","content":"An administrator configures a cryptographic engine and creates or imports a CA."},"976":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/overview-10","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/overview#from-onboarding-to-operation","content":"A DMS relates that CA to an enrollment policy."},"977":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/overview-11","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/overview#from-onboarding-to-operation","content":"The device generates a key and requests a certificate through EST, or an operator assigns it an identity."},"978":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/overview-12","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/overview#from-onboarding-to-operation","content":"Lamassu keeps the inventory, history and status of the identity."},"979":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/overview-13","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/overview#from-onboarding-to-operation","content":"Consumers check the chain and query OCSP or a CRL when they need to know whether it is still valid."},"980":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/overview-14","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/overview#from-onboarding-to-operation","content":"<Card title=\"Architecture\" description=\"Get to know the components and where each one's responsibility ends.\" href=\"/docs/platform/pki/concepts/architecture\" />"},"981":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/overview-15","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/overview#from-onboarding-to-operation","content":"<Card title=\"Identity lifecycle\" description=\"Follow a certificate from enrollment to renewal or revocation.\" href=\"/docs/platform/pki/concepts/certificate-lifecycle\" />"},"982":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model","type":"page","content":"Trust model","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Platform","Concepts"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model"},"983":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model","content":"Understand where trust originates, how it is distributed and what each component validates."},"984":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model#the-four-trust-decisions","content":"The four trust decisions"},"985":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model#who-can-issue","content":"Who can issue"},"986":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model-3","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model#what-can-be-issued","content":"What can be issued"},"987":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model-4","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model#who-can-request-it","content":"Who can request it"},"988":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model-5","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model#who-accepts-the-result","content":"Who accepts the result"},"989":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model-6","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model#identity-flow","content":"Identity flow"},"990":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model-7","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model#enrollment-validation-and-distribution-cas","content":"Enrollment, validation and distribution CAs"},"991":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model-8","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model#validation-and-revocation","content":"Validation and revocation"},"992":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model-9","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model#custody-limits","content":"Custody limits"},"993":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model-10","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model#recommended-pattern","content":"Recommended pattern"},"994":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model-11","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model","content":"In Lamassu, trust does not simply mean that a certificate exists in the inventory. A consumer trusts an identity when it can build a chain to a root it recognizes, check that the certificate is fit for the intended use and verify that it is still valid."},"995":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model-12","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model#who-can-issue","content":"The CA hierarchy defines which authorities can sign. A root CA establishes the anchor of trust; intermediate CAs separate operating domains and avoid using the root for every issuance."},"996":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model-13","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model#what-can-be-issued","content":"Certificate profiles limit validity, subject, uses, extensions and cryptographic parameters. Possessing a CA does not replace an issuance policy."},"997":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model-14","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model#who-can-request-it","content":"The DMS acts as the enrollment point. It can authenticate an EST request with a client certificate, an external webhook or a combination of both. CAs configured to validate the requester do not have to be the CA that will issue the new identity."},"998":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model-15","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model#who-accepts-the-result","content":"The consuming service or device keeps its own trust store. Lamassu can distribute the system CA, the enrollment CA and other managed CAs through `/cacerts`, but the consumer decides which ones it installs and how it applies validation."},"999":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model-16","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model#identity-flow","content":"The device proves it can enroll according to the DMS policy."},"1000":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model-17","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model#identity-flow","content":"The DMS validates the request and forwards the CSR to the enrollment CA."},"1001":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model-18","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model#identity-flow","content":"The CA applies the profile and signs without ever receiving the device's private key."},"1002":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model-19","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model#identity-flow","content":"The device installs the certificate and the chain it needs."},"1003":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model-20","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model#identity-flow","content":"The system that trusts the device validates the chain, dates, uses and revocation status."},"1004":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model-21","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model#identity-flow","content":"OIDC or X.509 identifies the operator calling Lamassu. The authorization service decides which actions it may perform. The X.509 hierarchy, on the other hand, determines whether a certificate presented by a device is trustworthy."},"1005":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model-22","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model#enrollment-validation-and-distribution-cas","content":"A DMS relates three sets that are worth designing separately:"},"1006":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model-23","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model#enrollment-validation-and-distribution-cas","content":"**Enrollment CA:** signs the new identities."},"1007":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model-24","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model#enrollment-validation-and-distribution-cas","content":"**Validation CAs:** authenticate the client certificates used for enrollment or migration. During re-enrollment, Lamassu tries the enrollment CA first and then the additional validation CAs."},"1008":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model-25","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model#enrollment-validation-and-distribution-cas","content":"**Distributed CAs:** form the content the device obtains through EST `/cacerts`. You can include the system CA, the enrollment CA and a list of managed CAs."},"1009":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model-26","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model#enrollment-validation-and-distribution-cas","content":"This separation makes it possible to migrate a fleet: you temporarily accept certificates from the old hierarchy, issue with the new one and distribute both chains during the overlap."},"1010":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model-27","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model#validation-and-revocation","content":"A valid chain does not by itself guarantee that a certificate should be accepted. The consumer must also check:"},"1011":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model-28","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model#validation-and-revocation","content":"that the current date is between `Not Before` and `Not After`;"},"1012":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model-29","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model#validation-and-revocation","content":"that `Key Usage` and `Extended Key Usage` allow the operation;"},"1013":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model-30","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model#validation-and-revocation","content":"that names, SANs and subject match the expected identity;"},"1014":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model-31","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model#validation-and-revocation","content":"that the certificate does not appear revoked in OCSP or a CRL."},"1015":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model-32","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model#validation-and-revocation","content":"During the mTLS authentication of a DMS, Lamassu attempts to check revocation. If the certificate does not contain enough information to perform that check, the backend logs a warning and continues treating it as not revoked. Design your profiles and distribution points to avoid that situation in production."},"1016":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model-33","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model#custody-limits","content":"The KMS keeps the reference to the key and delegates the operation to the configured engine. With an HSM or a cloud KMS, the private key can remain non-exportable. That protects custody, but it does not by itself prevent misuse: you still must restrict who can request a signature and audit those operations."},"1017":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model-34","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model#recommended-pattern","content":"Keep the root out of daily operations, or with very restricted access."},"1018":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model-35","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model#recommended-pattern","content":"Issue from intermediate CAs separated by environment or risk domain."},"1019":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model-36","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model#recommended-pattern","content":"Assign explicit profiles to every use case."},"1020":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model-37","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model#recommended-pattern","content":"Distribute the new trust before starting a rotation."},"1021":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model-38","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model#recommended-pattern","content":"Keep enough overlap to renew a disconnected fleet."},"1022":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model-39","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model#recommended-pattern","content":"Validate from the consuming system, not only from the Lamassu console."},"1023":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model-40","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/concepts/trust-model#recommended-pattern","content":"Continue with CA hierarchy and rotation to turn this model into an operating procedure."},"1024":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl","type":"page","content":"Revocation lists (CRL)","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Platform","Operate Lamassu"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl"},"1025":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl","content":"Generate and distribute signed lists to validate certificates offline."},"1026":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl#crl-service","content":"CRL service"},"1027":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl#va-role-and-per-ca-configuration","content":"VA role and per-CA configuration"},"1028":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl-3","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl#periodic-and-automatic-regeneration","content":"Periodic and automatic regeneration"},"1029":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl-4","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl#crl-contents","content":"CRL contents"},"1030":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl-5","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl#public-download-endpoint","content":"Public download endpoint"},"1031":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl-6","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl#va-role-management-api","content":"VA role management API"},"1032":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl-7","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl#from-the-interface","content":"From the interface"},"1033":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl-8","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl#references","content":"References"},"1034":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl-9","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl#crl-service","content":"A CRL (*Certificate Revocation List*) is a signed list containing the serial numbers of certificates revoked before their expiration date. Unlike OCSP, it does not require a real-time query: the relying party downloads the list periodically and consults it locally."},"1035":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl-10","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl#crl-service","content":"Lamassu generates and maintains one CRL per CA it manages. Each CRL is signed with the private key of the issuing CA itself and is stored in the object storage configured on the platform."},"1036":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl-11","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl#va-role-and-per-ca-configuration","content":"The publication of each CA's CRL is controlled by a *VA role*. This object defines how it is generated, when it is regenerated and which key signs it."},"1037":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl-12","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl#va-role-and-per-ca-configuration","content":"The main parameters are:"},"1038":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl-13","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl#va-role-and-per-ca-configuration","content":"**`validity`** defines the validity period reflected in `nextUpdate`. Its default value is 7 days."},"1039":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl-14","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl#va-role-and-per-ca-configuration","content":"**`refresh_interval`** sets the minimum interval between scheduled regenerations. By default it is approximately 6 days and 23 hours."},"1040":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl-15","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl#va-role-and-per-ca-configuration","content":"**`regenerate_on_revoke`** orders publishing a new version immediately after a revocation. It is enabled by default."},"1041":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl-16","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl#va-role-and-per-ca-configuration","content":"The `subject_key_id_signer` field identifies the CA whose private key signs the CRL. By default, each CA signs its own CRL."},"1042":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl-17","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl#va-role-and-per-ca-configuration","content":"Each CRL carries an incremental version number. Lamassu stores all versions under the path `pki/va/crl/{subject_key_id}/{version}.crl` in object storage."},"1043":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl-18","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl#periodic-and-automatic-regeneration","content":"A background process monitors active VA roles. When the remaining validity of the current CRL falls below the configured watch period (*blind period*), the system requests the generation of a new CRL. This prevents the published CRL from expiring without a valid version available."},"1044":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl-19","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl#periodic-and-automatic-regeneration","content":"Additionally, when `regenerate_on_revoke` is enabled, which is the default behavior, any certificate revocation immediately triggers the generation of a new CRL for the affected CA. This minimizes the time between revocation and its publication."},"1045":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl-20","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl#crl-contents","content":"Each entry of the CRL includes the serial number of the revoked certificate, the revocation date and the RFC 5280 reason code."},"1046":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl-21","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl#crl-contents","content":"The CRL also includes the *Issuing Distribution Point* (IDP, OID 2.5.29.28) extension, marked as critical, which indicates the public URL from which it can be downloaded. That URL points to the `/crl/{subject_key_id}` endpoint of each configured VA domain."},"1047":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl-22","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl#public-download-endpoint","content":"The latest CRL of a CA can be obtained directly without authentication:"},"1048":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl-23","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl#public-download-endpoint","content":"The response has `Content-Type: application/pkix-crl` and contains the CRL in DER format."},"1049":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl-24","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl#va-role-management-api","content":"The VA role of a CA can be queried and updated through the API:"},"1050":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl-25","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl#va-role-management-api","content":"Method"},"1051":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl-26","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-26/platform/pki/crl#va-role-management-api","content":"Path"},"1052":{"i